1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,170
Some say you can tell a lot about a person by the way they decorate their home.
有人说，从一个人装饰家的方式就能看出他的很多特质。

2
00:00:05,170 --> 00:00:15,060
We often find pleasure in the things we stick in our houses, be it trinket we bought on holiday, film memorabilium or painting to liven up walls.
我们总乐于在家中摆放一些物件，比如度假时买的小饰品、电影纪念品，或是能让墙面焕发生机的画作。

3
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:25,200
And when we head to others’ houses, we often see things we appreciate, but wouldn’t have in our own homes, because maybe they’re not quite to our taste.
当我们去别人家做客时，也常会看到一些自己欣赏、却不会放在自家的东西，可能只是因为这些东西不太合自己的口味。

4
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:30,140
The point is, the way we decorate our homes is very personal.
关键是，家装的方式极具个人色彩。

5
00:00:30,140 --> 00:00:36,640
And while many of us have plenty of stuff, there are always people who go that little bit further.
虽然我们很多人家里的东西已经不少，但总有人会想要更多。

6
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:43,110
So, when it comes to minimalism and maximalism, which one appeals to you more?
那么，说到极简主义和极繁主义这两种风格，你更偏爱哪一种呢？

7
00:00:43,110 --> 00:00:55,350
Minimalism was an art movement that started in the 1950s. Its basic principles are derived from a concept of ‘less is more’ – reducing things back to their most basic.
极简主义是20世纪50年代兴起的一场艺术运动，其基本原则源于“少即是多”的理念——将事物还原至最本质的状态。

8
00:00:55,350 --> 00:00:59,940
Some people took that art style and used it as a way of living.
一些人将这种艺术风格运用到了生活方式中。

9
00:00:59,940 --> 00:01:07,230
Ideas of vast open space with an organised and functional structure may spring to mind.
人们想到这种风格，往往会浮现出开阔敞亮、布局规整且实用性强的空间画面。

10
00:01:07,230 --> 00:01:16,060
They are usually decorated in simple pastel colour, with many minimalists opting for duotone, often just black and white.
这类家居通常采用简约的柔和色调，许多极简主义者还会选择双色搭配，通常就是黑与白。

11
00:01:16,060 --> 00:01:25,720
For some, especially maximalists, it may seem sparse and a bit bland to live without many things – even boring or depressing.
对有些人来说，尤其是极繁主义者，生活中少了很多物件，会显得空旷单调，甚至有些乏味沉闷。

12
00:01:25,720 --> 00:01:30,530
However, living in this way is seen by many as more practical.
但在很多人看来，这种生活方式其实更为实用。

13
00:01:30,530 --> 00:01:40,310
Maximalism is the opposite of minimalism and started in the 1970s. It embraces the core ideals that ‘more is more’.
极繁主义诞生于20世纪70年代，是极简主义的对立面，它信奉“多即是多”的核心理念。

14
00:01:40,310 --> 00:01:51,640
While minimalism centres around the principle of decluttering, it’s easy to imagine that a maximalist home is overflowing with items – but that’s not the base idea.
极简主义的核心是清理冗余物品，由此很容易让人联想到极繁主义的家会堆满各种物件——但这并非其本意。

15
00:01:51,640 --> 00:01:56,810
It’s more about filling the space – making the most of the area.
极繁主义更强调充实空间，充分利用每一处区域。

16
00:01:56,810 --> 00:02:03,070
Structured excess and bold colour combined with mixed pattern is what you will see in a home like this.
这种风格的家居，呈现出的是规整的繁复感、大胆的色彩运用以及多样的图案混搭。

17
00:02:03,070 --> 00:02:08,380
For a minimalist, used to more simplistic designs, it could be overwhelming.
对于习惯了简约设计的极简主义者而言，这样的空间可能会让人觉得眼花缭乱。

18
00:02:08,380 --> 00:02:13,280
But for those who embrace it, those things give a space personality.
但对钟爱极繁风格的人来说，这些元素恰恰赋予了空间独特的个性。

19
00:02:13,280 --> 00:02:16,670
The way you have your home is up to you!
家的风格终究由你做主！

20
00:02:16,670 --> 00:02:22,540
But, if you opt for maximalism, you may need to prepare for a bit more dusting.
不过，如果你选择了极繁主义，那可得做好多花些时间打扫除尘的准备。
